### A query key the entity does not declare is refused, never ignored. An ignored `?titel=…` answers
### with the whole collection and the caller has no way to notice they filtered nothing.
# @name UnknownKey
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/todos?colour=eq.red

### A misspelled operator is refused rather than falling back to `eq` — a mistyped operator that
### quietly became equality answers a different question than the caller asked.
# @name UnknownOperator
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/todos?status=equals.done

### `like` is a text operator, and `due_on` is a date. The operator exists and the field exists; the
### pairing does not, and that is checked rather than rendered into SQL and hoped for.
# @name OperatorWrongForType
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/todos?due_on=like.2026%25

### A paged read sorted by a NULLABLE field is refused: a keyset cursor cannot place its nulls. Every
### list here is paged, so this is `due_on`'s permanent state as a sort key (issue #116).
# @name SortByNullable
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/todos?order=due_on.asc&limit=2

### An unrecognised sort modifier is refused rather than ignored — an ignored one is a silent re-sort
# @name MalformedOrder
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/todos?order=title.sideways

### A page size past the configured maximum is refused, not quietly clamped — a clamped page makes a
### client's own arithmetic wrong, and an unbounded one is a denial of service one query long.
# @name PageTooLarge
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/todos?limit=5000

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Access. This project's five rules are all `true`, so there is nothing to authorize: every request
### above and below carries no credential at all, which is the point. What is left to pin is the ONE
### thing "no authorization" does not mean.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### A row created by nobody, so the reads below have something to find
# @name SeedRow
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/todos
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "{{runToken}}-open", "status": "todo" }

### Read it. No header, no key, no identity — and 200.
# @name ReadWithoutCredential
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/todos/{{SeedRow.response.body.$.id}}

### Write it, still anonymously. A `create` rule of `true` is evaluated against the candidate row and
### says yes, so the read/write asymmetry a role-based rule produces does not exist here.
# @name WriteWithoutCredential
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/todos/{{SeedRow.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "done" }

### And delete it, anonymously
# @name DeleteWithoutCredential
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [204]
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/todos/{{SeedRow.response.body.$.id}}

### The one thing that is NOT waived: a credential you actually presented has to work. Nothing here
### requires a key — but a request that offers a broken one is refused rather than treated as
### anonymous, because "this key is wrong" and "I have no key" are different situations with
### different fixes, and silently downgrading the first would hide a misconfigured client.
# @name BrokenKeyIsStillRefused
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [401]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/todos
X-Alvo-Api-Key: demo.0000000000000000

### A key that is not even key-shaped, same answer
# @name GarbageKeyIsStillRefused
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [401]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/todos
X-Alvo-Api-Key: nonsense

### An entity the descriptor does not declare has no route at all. Nothing is generated for it, so
### this is the web server's 404 rather than a policy decision — the descriptor IS the surface.
# @name UndeclaredEntity
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [404]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/projects

### An id that is not a guid does not match the route's `{id:guid}` constraint, so there is no
### endpoint to refuse it — the same 404, from the same place.
# @name NotAGuid
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [404]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/todos/not-a-guid

### A well-formed id nothing holds
# @name MissingRow
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [404]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/todos/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000
